====================GS Battery RAM usage====================Modification History: 7-Feb-91 Dave Lyons	Initial Release22-Feb-92 Dave Lyons	Documented $5F bits 1 and 2. 6-Apr-92 Dave Lyons	Allocated $63..64 for EtherTalk 4-Jun-92 Dave Lyons	Allocated $65 for Hierarchical Menu delay time 8-Jun-92 Dave Lyons	Allocated $66 for delay-until-hierarchical pop-up17-Sep-92 Dave Lyons	Added note on location $84 (mysterious).21-Oct-92 Dave Lyons	Fixed up $61, reserved bit 3 in $5F.12-Feb-93 Dave Lyons=============================================================================Here is a list of Battery-RAM locations beyond what's listed on page 14-12of Toolbox Reference Volume 1.  These reference numbers should be used withReadBParam and WriteBParam.A copy of the battery RAM can be found at $E1/02C0, and the Firmware looksthere directly.  System software should generally go through ReadBParam andWriteBParam rather than examining or changing the buffer directly.=============================================================================$59  Bit 7 on ROM3 auto-installs Visit Monitor and Memory Peeker CDAs at boot$5A  Key Translation (Event Manager)$5B  CloseView:	cvPowerMask equ %00001111 ; bits 0-3 (power)	cvUseKeys   equ %00010000 ; bit 4	cvMagnify   equ %00100000 ; bit 5	cvInvert    equ %01000000 ; bit 6	cvEnabled   equ %10000000 ; bit 7$5C  Not used???$5D  Not used???$5E  AUG_Param	bit 0 set means no closed captioning	bit 1 set means standard time clear if daylight savings time	bit 2 set means not to have auto daylight savings clear means to		 have auto daylight savings	bit 4-3 = amount of menu item blink (0..3)$5F  Toolbox miscellaneous use (6.0)         bits 7-6 = 10 if the byte has been initialized (default = $81)         bit    5 =          bit    4 =          bit    3 = (will be "don't put up AppleTalk config warnings" in 6.0.1)         bit    2 = 1 to make QDStartUp call SetIntUse(0)         bit    1 = 1 to suppress ShowBootInfo icons         bit    0 = 1 to alphabetize desk accessory lists$60  Toolbox: WaitUntil scaling$61  What network medium to use (1=LocalTalk, 2=EtherNet)$62  What OS to boot into (1=GS/OS, 2=ProDOS 8)  (Mark Day)$63..64  ¥not used¥ (Mark requested for network hints, but never used)$65  Drag delay for hierarchical menus (number of ticks you can be out of the         menu while moving diagonally before it "gives up" on you)$66  Delay in ticks until a hierarchical menu pops up.$67..68	Network number hint for Ethernet card (Wes Johnson)$69	Network node hint for Ethernet card (Wes)$80  AppleTalk Node Number$81  GS/OS Cache size$84  config_ram in device.dispatcher.src -- 2 units on generated devices?     This is very mysterious and undocumented.$A1-B6  At least one strange application messes with these locations.$FC-FF: Check Sum=============================================================================There is some remapping from logical to physical BRAM locations going on forROM 3.  Here is the interesting part of the table.  (Need to document thisbetter.)	dc.b $32	; $52 Disk Eject 1	dc.b $33	; $53 Disk Eject 2	dc.b $38	; $54 Reset RAM at next Reset	dc.b $3B	; $55 Delay To Start	dc.b $3C	; $56 Acceleration	dc.b $3D	; $57 Maximum Speed	dc.b $58	; $58 new Slot 1=============================================================================[end of document]